<h2 id="about">What this tool does</h2>
<p>Zakat becomes obligatory once your saved wealth — cash, bank balances, trade goods, gold and silver, and money owed to you, minus what you owe — stays above a minimum threshold called the nisab for a full lunar year. This calculator walks through exactly that: you list each asset, subtract liabilities, and it totals the zakat base, then applies the standard 2.5% rate to whatever clears the threshold. Nothing is transmitted; the maths is all in your browser.</p>
<p>Gold and silver need a price per gram to be worth anything in the nisab test, and those rates move daily. Rather than bake in a number that quietly goes stale, the page loads current indicative rates from a small configuration file the moment it opens, prints the date those rates were last updated, and lets you type over any of them so you can match today's market or a specific jeweller's quote. If the fetch ever fails, it falls back to safe built-in defaults and tells you so.</p>
<p>The nisab itself has two recognised measures: 87.48 grams of gold or 612.36 grams of silver. Many scholars use the lower silver threshold because it is more generous to recipients, so both are computed and shown, with your wealth compared against each. Once you see which nisab you clear and the resulting 2.5% figure, zakat becomes a concrete rupee amount rather than an estimate you hope is right.</p>
<h2 id="how-to-use">How to use the Zakat Calculator <span style="color:var(--cy)">| Step by Step Guide</span></h2>
<div class="howto"><ol><li><span>Review the loaded gold and silver rates (or type today's rates to override them) and choose 24K or 22K for your gold.</span></li><li><span>Enter cash in hand, bank savings, business inventory value and receivables you expect to collect.</span></li><li><span>Enter the grams of gold and of silver you own.</span></li><li><span>Subtract liabilities such as debts you must repay soon.</span></li><li><span>Press Calculate to see your nisab comparison and the 2.5% zakat due.</span></li></ol></div>
<span class="ru" data-ru lang="ros">Apna naqad, bank bachat, karobar ka maal, udhaar, sona (grams) aur chandi (grams) likhein, zimmedariyan (liabilities) minus karein. Sone/chandi ka rate zaroorat par khud badal lein. 'Calculate' dabane par nisab ka muwazna aur 2.5% zakat nazar aayega.</span>
<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
<ul class="feat-list"><li>Itemised wealth build-up: cash, savings, stock, gold, silver, receivables</li><li>Liabilities subtracted before the zakat base is measured</li><li>Gold priced per gram by 24K or 22K, silver per gram, all overridable</li><li>Both gold (87.48 g) and silver (612.36 g) nisab compared</li><li>Standard 2.5% zakat applied only once the threshold is cleared</li><li>Rates and currency load from a config file with a visible last-updated date</li></ul>
<h2 id="tips">Tips</h2>
<ul><li>Update the metal rates on the day you actually pay, not when you first opened the page.</li><li>Use the silver nisab if you follow scholars who prefer the lower, more inclusive threshold.</li><li>Count gold by weight at your karat rate; jewellery for wearing has separate fiqh opinions.</li><li>Receivables are usually zakat-liable only when reasonably collectable — exclude doubtful debts.</li><li>This is an aid to your own calculation; confirm anything unusual with a knowledgeable scholar.</li></ul>
<h2 id="faq">Frequently asked questions</h2>
<details><summary>How is the nisab decided here?</summary><p>Nisab equals the value of 87.48 grams of gold or 612.36 grams of silver. The tool values both at the rates you set and compares your net wealth against each, showing the lower silver-based threshold as the common reference.</p></details>
<details><summary>Why can I change the gold and silver rates?</summary><p>Metal prices change constantly and differ by market, so the loaded defaults are indicative only — verify current rates before paying zakat. You can override them with the live rate from a jeweller or your currency's market quote.</p></details>
<details><summary>Is the zakat calculator free to use?</summary><p>Yes — Zakat Calculator has no usage cap, no sign-up and no watermark, and it is not a trial: the page is a static file on https://wafasmart.tech with no billing backend behind it. </p></details>
<details><summary>What does the 2.5% apply to?</summary><p>Only the net zakat base — total zakatable assets minus liabilities — and only if that base meets or exceeds the nisab. Below nisab, zakat is not due.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does anything get uploaded when I use zakat calculator?</summary><p>No. Zakat Calculator reads your asset and liability figures straight into page memory, works on it locally and hands the result back as a download — there is no upload request to intercept, store or leak, and no log of what you processed.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can I use it on my phone?</summary><p>Yes. Zakat Calculator is mobile-first: one column, big tap targets, and the system keyboard opens with sensible number/text input. On iPhone, Files and the share sheet feed the picker the same way Downloads does on Android. The twelve fields stack into one column on a phone.</p></details>
